! Step 1 hand-back

Step 1 stays open at a design question. HEAD remains `fa5f50e16be2be4aaf8e06d3a3bf82dc65b74877`; no commit or push occurred. The lane carries two untracked red tests: `packages/lararium-node/tests/house-root-weld.test.ts` and `packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts/test_house_root.py`. The resolver inventory lives at `steps/step-001/resolver-inventory.txt` outside the worktree.

The requested layout names no acquired library location. `packages/lararium-node/src/library-store.ts` defaults to `larariumDataHome()/library`, and acquisition moves source bodies into that library by default. `packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts/testbeds/bed_manifest.py` mirrors that location. Mapping `larariumDataHome()` to `hearth` would put those acquired bodies inside the re-found deletion boundary. Mapping it to `projections` would also send sensoriums there unless their callers split, and the library holds acquired files rather than only deliberate plaintext projections. Options: place the acquired library under `projections/library` and explicitly preserve it; place it under `hearth/library` and include its contents in the R3 accept-loss inventory; or name another surviving house location. Lean: `projections/library`, with explicit TS/Python library resolvers and re-found preservation, because acquisition moves the source and those bytes may have no other copy. The operator's choice determines the library and reset boundary.

Red evidence: broker request 001 ran `house-root-weld.test.ts`, with two expected failures: unset `LAR_ROOT` did not throw and both languages still resolved `data/lares` instead of `hearth`. `python3 -m pytest packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts/test_house_root.py -q` failed because unset `LAR_ROOT` did not throw. The current weld covers vessel and identity only; expand it to the complete TS/Python resolver tables. No production resolver changed. Tests beyond these red checks remain unrun.

After a ruling, inventory callers of the broad helpers, implement the complete table and Python mirror together, switch affected test isolation to scratch `LAR_ROOT`, and run every affected file. Next relay request: 002. Step 2 and Step 3 remain owed; the Step 3 shim and compose changes need the controller's SHIP.

<<~/ahu>>

